<title>USA: Boston Life completes Phase III trial.</title>
<headline>Boston Life completes Phase III trial.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boston Life Sciences Inc said on Monday that it had completed its Phase III trial for Therafectin, the company's oral drug for the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis.</p>
<p>In a statement, the pharmaceutical company said results from the trial were expected within the next six to eight weeks.</p>
<p>The trial involved 218 patients at 25 sites in the United States and compared Therafectin to placebo in patients with active rheumatoid arthritis over a 20-week period, the company said.</p>
